Package: gorilla-portable-network-hub
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34)
Recommends: network-manager
Maintainer: gorillanobakaa <gorillanobakaa@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/gorillanobakaa-dot/Gorilla.Portable.Network.Hub
Description: Turn a laptop into the network and hand a folder to the room
 Creates a wifi network where none exists and hands a folder of files to
 every device in range. Built for classrooms with no internet, no router
 and often no mains power: the teacher's laptop becomes the access point
 and the children's machines need no account, no privileges and no setup.
 .
 Files are served in pieces that can be asked for individually, so a device
 that loses the signal carries on from where it stopped instead of starting
 the whole file again. Every piece can be checked against a fingerprint.
 .
 Run "hub" with no arguments for a screen; every command also works on its
 own. No dependencies at all beyond the C library, screen included.
 .
 Dual-track documentation, plain-language and developer, is installed under
 /usr/share/doc/gorilla-portable-network-hub.
